1
00:00:28,580 --> 00:00:29,980
SHIGEME

2
00:00:52,820 --> 00:00:56,460
It's been almost two years
since this game of death began.

3
00:00:57,420 --> 00:00:59,040
I'm still going it alone.

4
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,941
fighting solo on the front lines.

5
00:01:05,520 --> 00:01:08,760
Akihiko Kayaba's out
there somewhere, watching.

6
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:11,435
I wonder what he's thinking right now.

7
00:01:16,660 --> 00:01:17,895
Guess I'll head home.

8
00:01:43,960 --> 00:01:45,617
I don't know what I'm saying,

9
00:01:45,700 --> 00:01:52,437
but I don't know what I'm saying.

10
00:01:52,520 --> 00:01:58,320
I'm scared of the past,
I'm in the back of my head.

11
00:01:59,720 --> 00:02:03,320
I'm in the moment I'm

12
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:06,420
I'm in the sky,

13
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:08,580
I'm in the sky,

14
00:02:09,180 --> 00:02:11,600
I'm in the sky, I'm in the sky,

15
00:02:12,580 --> 00:02:18,740
I'm in the sky, Yeah, yeah, yeah,

16
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:26,040
yeah.

17
00:02:47,140 --> 00:02:50,320
This is the end of the game.

18
00:02:51,140 --> 00:02:54,197
I want to always be with you.

19
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:57,300
I'll give you everything I have.

20
00:03:21,340 --> 00:03:22,811
You've got to be kidding.

21
00:03:42,320 --> 00:03:43,520
No way.

22
00:03:44,340 --> 00:03:46,400
This is an Skills rare item.

23
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:50,398
Holy crap, this is the first
time I've ever seen one.

24
00:03:51,580 --> 00:03:55,051
Hey, Kirito, don't you already
have all the money you need?

25
00:03:55,480 --> 00:03:59,097
I'll buy it, but I'm saying, wouldn't
you rather have it for dinner?

26
00:03:59,180 --> 00:04:03,320
Sure, it's just, well, who knows
if I'll ever get another one.

27
00:04:03,420 --> 00:04:05,260
So keep it. What's the point?

28
00:04:05,940 --> 00:04:10,705
Look, to prepare an item like this, you
need to have a high enough cooking skill.

29
00:04:10,820 --> 00:04:11,938
Yeah, you're right.

30
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:13,668
If we try, we just burn it.

31
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:17,320
Hmm... Kirito.

32
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:24,620
I've got my chef.

33
00:04:24,900 --> 00:04:26,060
Uh, what chef?

34
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:30,380
Hey, Asuna's here.

35
00:04:30,640 --> 00:04:33,405
Seeing you in a dump like
this is beyond weird.

36
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:34,580
Oh, save it.

37
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:36,517
I came to see if you were still alive.

38
00:04:36,600 --> 00:04:39,017
You know, it's almost time
for the next boss raid.

39
00:04:39,100 --> 00:04:40,397
I'm on your friend list.

40
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:42,397
If you want to know I'm
alive, just check that.

41
00:04:42,480 --> 00:04:44,600
Whatever, now I know you're alive.

42
00:04:45,140 --> 00:04:46,728
Anyway, what are you up to?

43
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:48,697
What's all this about a chef?

44
00:04:48,780 --> 00:04:50,040
Oh, yeah, that.

45
00:04:50,320 --> 00:04:53,202
I was wondering what your
cooking skill level is.

46
00:04:54,260 --> 00:04:55,090
Hmm.

47
00:04:55,173 --> 00:04:56,980
Totally maxed it out last week. What?

48
00:04:57,440 --> 00:04:58,280
Cool, huh?

49
00:04:59,060 --> 00:05:01,740
Well, if you're that good, I need a favor.

50
00:05:07,900 --> 00:05:10,297
You got a Rika Rabbit?

51
00:05:10,380 --> 00:05:13,517
I'll trade you all you have
to do is cook it up for me,

52
00:05:13,600 --> 00:05:15,718
and I'll let you have a little bite.

53
00:05:19,500 --> 00:05:20,330
Yeah.

54
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:29,937
Sorry pal, you heard the lady?

55
00:05:30,020 --> 00:05:33,477
Guess I'm keeping it, yeah, but you
could at least let me taste it right?

56
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:35,157
I thought we were tight man.

57
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:38,475
I'll write a review for you,
but only two pages promise

58
00:05:40,380 --> 00:05:41,980
Damn, that is cold.

59
00:05:43,580 --> 00:05:45,760
So, where am I going to cook it?

60
00:05:47,140 --> 00:05:48,097
Okay, well...

61
00:05:48,180 --> 00:05:50,177
I'm guessing not your place, right?

62
00:05:50,260 --> 00:05:51,789
You even own any cookware?

63
00:05:53,280 --> 00:05:54,110
Okay,

64
00:05:54,193 --> 00:05:56,037
because the main ingredient is special,

65
00:05:56,120 --> 00:05:59,238
I won't have a problem if
we used my place this time.

66
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:02,360
Thank you for escorting me.

67
00:06:02,900 --> 00:06:03,800
You may go.

68
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:08,986
I'm sorry, ma 'am, but I can't allow you
to go home with such a shady character.

69
00:06:10,900 --> 00:06:15,135
I don't know the extent of his
shadiness, but I know he's quite skilled.

70
00:06:15,220 --> 00:06:18,280
In fact, he's ten levels
above you, Kuradeel.

71
00:06:18,620 --> 00:06:21,180
Are you implying I'm inferior to him?

72
00:06:22,060 --> 00:06:23,120
Oh, I know.

73
00:06:23,380 --> 00:06:25,498
He's one of those beaters, isn't he?

74
00:06:26,340 --> 00:06:27,170
Yeah.

75
00:06:27,253 --> 00:06:28,120
What if I am?

76
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:29,917
You shouldn't go with him, ma 'am.

77
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:32,237
All him and his kind care
about are themselves.

78
00:06:32,320 --> 00:06:35,791
You can't expect anything good
to come from scum like that.

79
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:37,600
Hey, what's going on?

80
00:06:37,900 --> 00:06:39,217
That's Lightning Flash Asuna.

81
00:06:39,300 --> 00:06:40,300
You're right.

82
00:06:40,560 --> 00:06:41,619
She's really cute.

83
00:06:42,300 --> 00:06:44,860
Listen, I'm second in command here.

84
00:06:45,120 --> 00:06:47,060
I am ordering you to go home.

85
00:06:49,860 --> 00:06:51,880
Are you sure about this?

86
00:06:52,100 --> 00:06:53,040
Of course.

87
00:07:03,460 --> 00:07:04,290
Whoa.

88
00:07:04,373 --> 00:07:05,886
There's hardly anyone around.

89
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:08,117
It's really cool.

90
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:11,024
If you like it so much,
why don't you move here?

91
00:07:11,540 --> 00:07:12,370
I don't know.

92
00:07:12,453 --> 00:07:14,889
This floor seems way
out of my price range.

93
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:18,217
Anyway, what's the deal
with that guy back there?

94
00:07:18,300 --> 00:07:20,241
He was mad-dogging me like crazy.

95
00:07:20,640 --> 00:07:22,340
Oh, he's just my bodyguard.

96
00:07:22,740 --> 00:07:26,622
The Guild's new policy says all
higher-ups have to have an escort.

97
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:28,550
It's lame.

98
00:07:28,780 --> 00:07:31,557
The Guild didn't have all these
rules and regulations before.

99
00:07:31,640 --> 00:07:33,228
We used to be really small.

100
00:07:33,860 --> 00:07:36,377
But then, more and more people joined up.

101
00:07:36,460 --> 00:07:41,225
After that, when we became the strongest
guild, everything started getting weird.

102
00:07:44,060 --> 00:07:47,648
Well, I'm probably making a
bigger deal out of it than it is.

103
00:07:48,460 --> 00:07:49,872
Anyway, we better hurry.

104
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:51,019
It's getting dark.

105
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:52,200
Oh, okay.

106
00:07:56,300 --> 00:07:58,460
Wow, you've got a killer pad.

107
00:08:01,640 --> 00:08:04,180
Hey, how much did all this cost?

108
00:08:06,460 --> 00:08:09,813
The room and the furniture
cost around four million coal.

109
00:08:10,020 --> 00:08:11,785
Anyway, make yourself at home.

110
00:08:12,560 --> 00:08:13,560
Uh, sure.

111
00:08:15,980 --> 00:08:17,020
Holy moly.

112
00:08:19,140 --> 00:08:20,180
Four million.

113
00:08:20,920 --> 00:08:22,620
Man, that's a lot of coal.

114
00:08:23,640 --> 00:08:27,522
I'm sure I've earned that much,
too, but blowing it all on a flat?

115
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:36,428
Are you going to take
off your coat or what?

116
00:08:37,180 --> 00:08:38,620
Oh, yeah, sorry.

117
00:08:43,680 --> 00:08:46,400
So this is a legendary Skills ingredient.

118
00:08:47,160 --> 00:08:49,237
Okay, how do you want this cooked up?

119
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:52,017
I thought I'd leave that
decision up to the chef.

120
00:08:52,100 --> 00:08:55,520
In that case, how about
we make it into a stew?

121
00:08:56,600 --> 00:08:57,430
Ragoom.

122
00:08:57,560 --> 00:09:00,148
That's pretty much the
definition of a stew.

123
00:09:11,420 --> 00:09:15,479
In real life, there'd be a lot more
steps involved in preparing this.

124
00:09:17,060 --> 00:09:18,880
Cooking an SAO is so simple.

125
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:21,454
Believe it or not, it's kind of boring.

126
00:09:23,740 --> 00:09:25,152
That takes care of that.

127
00:09:25,320 --> 00:09:26,614
Now for the next step.

128
00:09:27,020 --> 00:09:29,902
I was thinking about making
a couple side dishes.

129
00:09:55,880 --> 00:10:00,645
I've been here two years and this is the
first time I've ever eaten Skills food.

130
00:10:00,960 --> 00:10:03,880
I'm so happy I survived
long enough to eat that.

131
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:05,580
Yeah, me too.

132
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:08,240
It's so weird.

133
00:10:09,360 --> 00:10:10,617
Sometimes, I don't know,

134
00:10:10,700 --> 00:10:14,157
I get this feeling that like
I've lived here my entire life.

135
00:10:14,240 --> 00:10:15,652
You ever feel like that?

136
00:10:16,060 --> 00:10:17,740
Yeah, almost all the time.

137
00:10:18,320 --> 00:10:21,657
In fact, there's days I don't even
think about the real world at all.

138
00:10:21,740 --> 00:10:23,140
And it's not just me.

139
00:10:23,840 --> 00:10:24,670
These days,

140
00:10:24,753 --> 00:10:26,237
more and more people
don't seem to care about

141
00:10:26,320 --> 00:10:29,357
clearing the game and getting
back to the real world.

142
00:10:29,440 --> 00:10:33,157
I notice there's not that many players
out there fighting on the front lines.

143
00:10:33,240 --> 00:10:35,100
Maybe 500, if that.

144
00:10:36,300 --> 00:10:38,377
I guess they're used to it.

145
00:10:38,460 --> 00:10:39,872
They don't care anymore.

146
00:10:42,160 --> 00:10:44,340
Yeah, well, I want to go back.

147
00:10:45,580 --> 00:10:48,200
I mean, there's things I haven't done yet.

148
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:49,340
I have to.

149
00:10:50,360 --> 00:10:51,580
I know how you feel.

150
00:10:51,820 --> 00:10:55,137
And when you stop to consider
it, there's everyone else, right?

151
00:10:55,220 --> 00:10:57,097
All the people who still count on us?

152
00:10:57,180 --> 00:10:59,356
If we give up, it's not fair to them.

153
00:11:04,400 --> 00:11:08,577
Don't go there what I've
seen that same look on guys

154
00:11:08,660 --> 00:11:11,954
faces before and always right
before they proposed to me

155
00:11:14,860 --> 00:11:16,360
You should see your face.

156
00:11:16,500 --> 00:11:18,912
I guess you never had a girlfriend before

157
00:11:19,860 --> 00:11:21,100
Yeah, whatever.

158
00:11:21,300 --> 00:11:22,300
I'm a solo player

159
00:11:28,400 --> 00:11:29,940
And you're okay with that?

160
00:11:30,120 --> 00:11:32,238
You don't ever want to join a guild?

161
00:11:33,020 --> 00:11:36,373
I know how the beta players
don't fit in with the guilds.

162
00:11:36,560 --> 00:11:41,880
But ever since we got to Floor 70,
things are getting more dangerous.

163
00:11:42,400 --> 00:11:45,165
The monster algorithms
are even more irregular.

164
00:11:48,140 --> 00:11:50,728
There are things a solo
player can't handle.

165
00:11:51,260 --> 00:11:52,319
Unexpected things.

166
00:11:52,940 --> 00:11:55,234
Sometimes, warping out isn't an option.

167
00:11:55,800 --> 00:11:57,860
Yeah, well, I'm pretty careful.

168
00:11:59,020 --> 00:12:01,000
I work better by myself anyway.

169
00:12:01,540 --> 00:12:05,357
Besides, most of the time, instead of
helping, party members just get in the way.

170
00:12:05,440 --> 00:12:06,270
Oh, yeah?

171
00:12:09,460 --> 00:12:10,290
My bad.

172
00:12:10,373 --> 00:12:12,420
Everyone except for you. Good.

173
00:12:14,200 --> 00:12:16,900
So, what do you say you
and me team up again?

174
00:12:18,160 --> 00:12:20,457
Black's my lucky color this week anyway.

175
00:12:20,540 --> 00:12:21,370
Hold up a sec.

176
00:12:21,660 --> 00:12:23,517
Don't you have stuff you
have to do for your guild?

177
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:24,797
You can't just bail on him.

178
00:12:24,880 --> 00:12:27,317
It's not like we have any
leveling quotas to meet.

179
00:12:27,400 --> 00:12:29,117
Well, then what about your bodyguard?

180
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:30,376
I'll just ditch him.

181
00:12:54,400 --> 00:12:56,635
The front lines are dangerous, though.

182
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:03,240
Okay, fine.

183
00:13:10,100 --> 00:13:14,800
Well, I suppose thanks are in
order for the meal, so thank you.

184
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:16,760
Thank you for cooking it.

185
00:13:16,880 --> 00:13:17,821
Maybe next time.

186
00:13:18,120 --> 00:13:19,237
What am I saying?

187
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:22,438
I'll never get my hands on
something like that again.

188
00:13:22,540 --> 00:13:23,370
No way.

189
00:13:23,453 --> 00:13:26,491
You can make anything yummy if
you have the skills to cook.

190
00:13:31,480 --> 00:13:36,360
Looking at this world and seeing
what it's become since we got here,

191
00:13:36,620 --> 00:13:39,679
is this really what Akihiko
Kayaba wanted to create?

192
00:13:50,320 --> 00:13:51,150
Where is she?

193
00:13:56,840 --> 00:13:57,670
No!

194
00:13:57,753 --> 00:13:58,583
Watch out!

195
00:14:03,280 --> 00:14:05,960
What is this thing?

196
00:14:07,180 --> 00:14:08,540
Hmm, squishy.

197
00:14:19,780 --> 00:14:20,610
Ow.

198
00:14:31,580 --> 00:14:32,410
Um, hey.

199
00:14:32,680 --> 00:14:33,856
Good morning, Asuna.

200
00:14:40,560 --> 00:14:41,460
What's wrong?

201
00:14:44,920 --> 00:14:46,957
Why are you behaving like this, ma 'am?

202
00:14:47,040 --> 00:14:48,569
I'm only following orders.

203
00:14:49,020 --> 00:14:51,137
Please, let's go back to headquarters.

204
00:14:51,220 --> 00:14:53,580
I won't, especially not with you.

205
00:14:53,820 --> 00:14:57,017
And why were you lurking around
my house in the morning, huh?

206
00:14:57,100 --> 00:15:00,159
You have a bad habit of
leaving without any warning.

207
00:15:00,360 --> 00:15:01,557
So for the past month,

208
00:15:01,640 --> 00:15:04,497
part of my mission has been to
keep an eye on you in Selmburg.

209
00:15:04,580 --> 00:15:05,410
What?

210
00:15:05,493 --> 00:15:06,323
Who ordered this?

211
00:15:06,460 --> 00:15:07,837
It wasn't the commander.

212
00:15:07,920 --> 00:15:10,977
With all due respect, ma 'am,
my mission is to guard you.

213
00:15:11,060 --> 00:15:13,537
No matter where you are,
including your home.

214
00:15:13,620 --> 00:15:15,149
No, it doesn't, you idiot!

215
00:15:16,620 --> 00:15:20,561
I wish you would be a little more
understanding about this, ma 'am.

216
00:15:21,040 --> 00:15:23,334
Now then, let's return to headquarters.

217
00:15:28,820 --> 00:15:31,877
Sorry, but I'll be borrowing your
second-in-command for the day,

218
00:15:31,960 --> 00:15:34,489
so you'll just have to
make do without her.

219
00:15:34,860 --> 00:15:37,331
I'll take responsibility for her security.

220
00:15:37,940 --> 00:15:40,697
Don't worry, it's not like
we're going on a boss raid.

221
00:15:40,780 --> 00:15:42,839
You can go, she'll be fine with me.

222
00:15:43,320 --> 00:15:44,150
Insolent punk!

223
00:15:44,420 --> 00:15:46,080
Do you know who I am?

224
00:15:46,200 --> 00:15:48,957
I'm a member of the Glorious
Knights of the Blood Oath!

225
00:15:49,040 --> 00:15:51,697
A low-level player like
you couldn't protect her!

226
00:15:51,780 --> 00:15:53,956
I can do a better job of it than you.

227
00:15:56,240 --> 00:15:57,940
You've got a big mouth, kid.

228
00:15:58,220 --> 00:16:02,514
So I'm going to give you a chance to
prove just how tough you really are.

229
00:16:08,040 --> 00:16:09,000
Are you sure?

230
00:16:09,900 --> 00:16:10,917
Don't worry.

231
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:13,471
I'll tell the commander how this happened.

232
00:16:19,140 --> 00:16:21,377
Please move to a safe distance, ma 'am.

233
00:16:21,460 --> 00:16:26,107
I'm going to prove beyond any doubt that
I am the only one who can protect you.

234
00:16:30,240 --> 00:16:33,437
Kirito's gonna duel a guy from
the Knights of the Blood Oath.

235
00:16:33,520 --> 00:16:34,932
This'll be fun to watch.

236
00:17:05,180 --> 00:17:06,010
Ha, ha, ha.

237
00:17:20,100 --> 00:17:21,680
I can't believe it!

238
00:17:27,940 --> 00:17:30,220
Holy crap, he destroyed his sword.

239
00:17:30,460 --> 00:17:31,578
How did he do that?

240
00:17:32,700 --> 00:17:36,617
If you want to try again with another
weapon, I'll be glad to take you on.

241
00:17:36,700 --> 00:17:38,300
Or we can call it a day.

242
00:17:48,220 --> 00:17:49,050
Asuna!

243
00:17:51,640 --> 00:17:53,700
I don't know how, but he cheated!

244
00:17:53,980 --> 00:17:55,980
You saw how he destroyed my sword!

245
00:17:56,080 --> 00:17:58,017
He must have used some kind of trick!

246
00:17:58,100 --> 00:18:02,159
There's no other way I could have
lost to a pathetic beater like him!

247
00:18:03,320 --> 00:18:04,150
Kuradeel,

248
00:18:04,280 --> 00:18:06,937
as second in command of the
Knights of the Blood Oath,

249
00:18:07,020 --> 00:18:09,920
I'm relieving you of your
duties as my bodyguard.

250
00:18:10,400 --> 00:18:13,988
You're to return to headquarters
and wait for further orders.

251
00:18:14,600 --> 00:18:16,200
You can't be serious.

252
00:18:16,620 --> 00:18:17,580
Damn you.

253
00:18:31,400 --> 00:18:32,230
Teleport.

254
00:18:32,660 --> 00:18:33,490
Gransom.

255
00:18:47,300 --> 00:18:48,380
I'm so sorry.

256
00:18:48,740 --> 00:18:50,858
I didn't mean to drag you into that.

257
00:18:50,980 --> 00:18:52,340
No, it's no big deal.

258
00:18:52,680 --> 00:18:55,140
I'm worried about you. Are you okay?

259
00:18:56,300 --> 00:18:57,130
Yeah, I am.

260
00:18:57,213 --> 00:18:59,297
The Guild's getting on my nerves is all.

261
00:18:59,380 --> 00:19:02,297
Maybe because I've been so
focused on clearing the game.

262
00:19:02,380 --> 00:19:06,380
Or maybe because I'm so demanding
of the other members in the Guild.

263
00:19:07,680 --> 00:19:08,800
Yeah, I get that.

264
00:19:09,240 --> 00:19:11,317
But you didn't have much of a choice.

265
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:12,230
Think about it.

266
00:19:12,313 --> 00:19:13,817
If you'd done things any different,

267
00:19:13,900 --> 00:19:17,371
you think your guild would have
gotten as far as they have?

268
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:20,020
I mean, what do I know?

269
00:19:20,140 --> 00:19:22,669
I just mess around as
a solo player, right?

270
00:19:23,760 --> 00:19:28,289
The thing is, if you take a day off to
team up with a loser like me, so what?

271
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:29,757
That's your decision to make.

272
00:19:29,840 --> 00:19:32,337
In my opinion, no one's
got the right to complain.

273
00:19:32,420 --> 00:19:33,250
Screw them.

274
00:19:36,960 --> 00:19:39,725
Wow, thank you for your
opinion on the subject.

275
00:19:40,040 --> 00:19:43,437
OK, I accept your offer and I'll
be taking a day off from the guild.

276
00:19:43,520 --> 00:19:45,057
You can play forward today.

277
00:19:45,140 --> 00:19:45,970
Huh?

278
00:19:46,053 --> 00:19:46,883
Wait a second.

279
00:19:46,966 --> 00:19:48,697
Aren't we supposed to
take turns as forward?

280
00:19:48,780 --> 00:19:50,760
Sorry, it's my day off, remember?

281
00:19:51,120 --> 00:19:52,120
Oh, come on!

282
00:20:19,040 --> 00:20:22,617
Having someone along who knows how
to fight sure makes things easier.

283
00:20:22,700 --> 00:20:24,053
Switch with me, Kirito!

284
00:20:24,520 --> 00:20:25,420
Yeah, right!

285
00:20:44,300 --> 00:20:45,540
Kirito, look.

286
00:20:53,440 --> 00:20:55,300
Is that what I think it is?

287
00:20:55,940 --> 00:20:56,770
Uh-huh.

288
00:20:57,840 --> 00:20:59,620
We found the boss room.

289
00:21:00,460 --> 00:21:01,557
What do we do?

290
00:21:01,640 --> 00:21:03,780
So, you think we should look inside?

291
00:21:04,500 --> 00:21:06,088
Well, we came all this way.

292
00:21:06,360 --> 00:21:09,097
Besides, boss monsters never
leave the rooms they guard.

293
00:21:09,180 --> 00:21:11,827
I think we'll be okay
if we just take a peek.

294
00:21:12,200 --> 00:21:13,030
Okay.

295
00:21:13,420 --> 00:21:16,300
Have a teleport crystal
ready, just in case.

296
00:21:16,880 --> 00:21:17,710
Right.

297
00:21:19,680 --> 00:21:22,020
Okay, are you ready? Mm-hmm.

298
00:22:01,640 --> 00:22:03,697
We're here, we're here. I

299
00:22:03,780 --> 00:22:10,780
heard

300
00:22:19,060 --> 00:22:19,890
the sound of

301
00:22:19,973 --> 00:22:20,803
the sound of the sound.

302
00:22:21,799 --> 00:22:23,637
I heard the sound of the sound.

303
00:22:23,720 --> 00:22:29,040
It's a little sad to me. Yeah,

304
00:22:29,540 --> 00:22:30,977
yeah, yeah,

305
00:22:31,060 --> 00:22:38,060
yeah,

306
00:22:41,960 --> 00:22:48,960
yeah.

307
00:22:59,340 --> 00:23:02,577
I can't believe this love.

308
00:23:02,660 --> 00:23:05,100
In the front of my eyes,

309
00:23:05,540 --> 00:23:09,940
I can't believe it.

310
00:23:13,180 --> 00:23:17,220
Even if I'm dreaming, I can't believe it.

311
00:23:17,900 --> 00:23:20,677
I'm still in the middle of my heart.

312
00:23:35,520 --> 00:23:37,860
Next time, the blue-eyed demon.
